 "note": "Indonesia's largest banks are BRI, Mandiri, BCA and BNI. Mandiri's product summary (RIPLAY, versi umum, read 2026-10-30) gives its common terms (1.75% a month on purchases and cash, a cash advance 6% or 150,000 rupiah, a late payment 1% of the bill at most 100,000, the minimum 5% or 50,000, over the limit 150,000) but leaves each card's membership fee to the card chosen, without a figure, so no Mandiri card is written; BRI's and BNI's card summaries weren't reached in this pass. BCA's product summary for its credit cards (RIPLAY, in force from 19 August 2026, read again 2026-10-30): purchases and cash 1.75% a month; each card's main-card annual fee: 125,000 rupiah for the Everyday, UnionPay, tiket.com, Blibli, Visa Batman and Mastercard Globe cards, 250,000 for BCA Card Platinum, 450,000 for the JCB, Visa and Mastercard Black, 500,000 for the KrisFlyer Visa Signature, 1,000,000 for the KrisFlyer Visa Infinite and Mastercard World, 2,000,000 for the PPS Club Visa Infinite, and none for BCA Kartu Kredit Indonesia (the QR-only card issued alongside a BCA Card, with no cash advance); a cash advance 3% (Everyday and Platinum) or 4% of the amount, at least 40,000 rupiah, the summary's range read that way; over the limit up to 40,000 rupiah, nothing on the Platinum to KKI cards, written as 40,000 on the six others; a late payment 1% of the total bill, at most 100,000 (written as a share of the balance); the minimum payment 5% of the bill. The 20,000-rupiah counter fee on a cash advance, stamp duty, card replacement and statement fees aren't written. The summary states no foreign-transaction fee or grace period.",
